        {
          "section": null,
          "text": "The associate of arts degree in general studies requires 39 credits in the student’s chosen area of specialization or electives, plus 21 credits of core curriculum including: one theology core, one philosophy core, one history or social science or American founding principles core, one natural science core, one literature core (ENG 211), one Catholic traditions in fine arts core, and one math or economics core.",
          "codes": [
